drm/amd/display: scaled modes on the stitched Apple 5K panel

Applies ON TOP of imac5k-stitch-layer-7.x.patch (and the patches after it).

The stitched root runs one timing only: both tiles at their native
2560x2880. Before this patch any other crtc mode was either rejected
("atomic reject non-stitched root mode", e.g. when the screen wakes at a
non-native mode) or, while the stitched stream was live, accepted as a
logical mode without being scaled: the plane split only ran for a
framebuffer two tiles wide, so a 3840x2160 desktop showed squashed on the
left tile with the right tile black.

A smaller mode is now a logical mode, the way amdgpu scales a smaller mode
onto an ordinary eDP panel:

  * modes: the stitched mode stays preferred; common smaller sizes
    (3840x2160, 3200x1800, 2880x1620, 2560x1600, 2560x1440, ... 1280x720)
    are listed beside it, each the stitched mode with a smaller active
    area. mode_valid accepts any size from 640x360 up to the panel's,
    validated on the native timing it will run on.
  * streams: a scaled mode builds its stream from the native stitched
    mode, so both tiles keep their native timing, also on a fresh enable
    (wake from DPMS off). A live switch between usable modes stays the
    logical modeset it was, now limited to modes the panel can show. The
    root stream stays 1:1 whatever the crtc mode, and the peer stream is
    added whenever the root carries the tile timing.
  * planes: the primary plane is placed on the panel by the connector's
    scaling property (aspect-fit by default; full and center honoured),
    as set in the commit (kept in dm_crtc_state, so atomic check and
    commit place it alike), and split at the tile seam into a left and a right source window, each
    scaled onto its tile -- in the modeset path and on every flip. For the
    stitched mode this is the plain halving it always was. Each window
    starts exactly at its src_rect.x, because DCE programs the cursor
    relative to that offset.
  * cursor: the DCE cursor is blended before the scaler, in source pixels,
    so it scales with the plane and its position stays in crtc mode
    coordinates. The right-tile copy moves left by the width of the root's
    source window (the tile width at the stitched mode, 1920 at 3840x2160),
    not by a fixed tile width.

